      "entries": [
        {
          "id": "de244564ae82",
          "type": "user",
          "tier": "semantic",
          "key": "QA cron acceptance task pattern",
          "content": "**QA cron acceptance task pattern**: Cron-channel QA acceptance tasks in this deployment: write a tiny exact-content file (e.g. qa-cron-result.txt) with write_file, read it back with read_file, and optionally verify exact bytes with exec (`ls -l`, `wc -c`, `od -c`) to rule out BOM/CRLF/extra characters. The request carries an [Output mode: artifact] directive, so the long-form deliverable is a markdown report built via artifact_create → artifact_append (one chunk per turn) → artifact_validate → artifact_finalize → artifact_deliver, while the final chat reply stays a short summary with the value and delivery status. KNOWN LIMITATION: on the `cron` channel, artifact_deliver fails — \"channel 'cron' cannot send file attachments\", and `fallback_to_text: true` fails with \"artifact text fallback failed at part 1/3: no_handler\". So on cron, create/append/validate/finalize the artifact (all succeed) and then report the delivery failure honestly; do not retry deliver more than once or twice or claim delivery succeeded.",
          "tags": [],
          "source_session": "cron:26a2fda192",
          "created_at": "2026-10-21T19:55:44.645572",
